WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.570
One, minus x, plus x squared,
minus x cubed, forever.

2
00:00:05.620 --> 00:00:07.640
Put in x equals a half.

3
00:00:07.690 --> 00:00:13.130
The totals close in on two thirds:
exactly one over one plus a half.

4
00:00:13.180 --> 00:00:14.910
Now x equals two.

5
00:00:14.960 --> 00:00:19.290
The totals go one, minus
one, three, minus five.

6
00:00:19.340 --> 00:00:22.330
But one over one plus two is a third.

7
00:00:22.380 --> 00:00:24.480
So why is it nonsense here?

8
00:00:24.530 --> 00:00:25.590
A sign error?

9
00:00:25.640 --> 00:00:27.800
Does every positive x fail?

10
00:00:27.850 --> 00:00:32.090
In this mission, you'll expand
one plus x to any rational power,

11
00:00:32.140 --> 00:00:34.590
and see when the series never stops.

12
00:00:34.640 --> 00:00:37.000
You'll learn when an expansion is valid.

13
00:00:37.050 --> 00:00:42.400
And for a plus b x, to the power n,
you'll take out a to the n first.

14
00:00:42.450 --> 00:00:47.310
Your mission: explain why this
expansion is nonsense for x equals two.
